&lt;!-- more --&gt;</content><category term="Programming"></category><category term="rest"></category><category term="python"></category><category term="webservice"></category></entry><entry><title>Linux command line sort on dates</title><link href="https://blog.florijnconsultancy.nl/articles/linux-command-line-sort-on-dates.html" rel="alternate"></link><published>2015-04-24T14:38:00+02:00</published><updated>2015-04-24T14:38:00+02:00</updated><author><name>Peter Florijn</name></author><id>tag:blog.florijnconsultancy.nl,2015-04-24:/articles/linux-command-line-sort-on-dates.html</id><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;linux command line sort on&amp;nbsp;dates&lt;/p&gt;</summary><content type="html">&lt;p&gt;For one of my projects I needed to sort a csv file on a date field with dd/mm/yyyy&amp;nbsp;format.&lt;/p&gt;
